window.NEO_FIELDKIT={"unit":"percentages-ratio-growth-bounds","expedition":"The Market Hall","tools":[{"title":"Ratio bar","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"38\" width=\"32\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#c98a3a\" stroke=\"#6b4a1f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"42\" y=\"38\" width=\"48\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#b0412f\" stroke=\"#6b2a1f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M26 38V62M58 38V62M74 38V62\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">2</text><text x=\"66\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">3</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">2 : 3</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>Simplify a ratio by dividing both parts by the same number.</b></p><p>10 : 25: both divide by 5, so 10 : 25 = 2 : 5.</p><p>Keep the order: the first part stays first.</p>","room":"The Spice Stall","lesson":"Lesson 1 · Ratio, sharing and the unitary method"},{"title":"Unit price card","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"20\" width=\"72\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3e6c4\" stroke=\"#8a6d40\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">1 bag</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">£ ?</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>Find one, then scale.</b></p><p>4 tins cost £2.80. One tin costs £2.80 ÷ 4 = £0.70, so 7 tins cost 7 × £0.70 = £4.90.</p>","room":"The Bulk Bin","lesson":"Lesson 2 · Direct and inverse proportion"},{"title":"Percentage line","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M10 60 H90\" stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M10 52V68M50 52V68M90 52V68\" stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">0%</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">50%</text><text x=\"88\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">100%</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">0</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">0.5</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">1</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>A percentage is a number out of 100.</b></p><p>40% = 40/100 = 0.4. So 40% of £50 is 0.4 × 50 = £20.</p><p>Or build it: 10% of £50 is £5, so 40% is 4 × £5 = £20.</p>","room":"The Sale Rail","lesson":"Lesson 3 · Percentages as multipliers"},{"title":"Before-and-after bars","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"56\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#7fb6e0\" stroke=\"#2f4f6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"56\" y=\"42\" width=\"30\" height=\"44\" fill=\"#f2c14e\" stroke=\"#8f6a26\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M56 56H86\" stroke=\"#8f6a26\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"29\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">old</text><text x=\"71\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">new</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>The change is the difference between the new and the old.</b></p><p>A ticket went from £40 to £46: the change is £46 − £40 = £6.</p><p>Compared with the old price, £6 out of £40 is 6 ÷ 40 = 0.15, which is 15%.</p>","room":"The Price Board","lesson":"Lesson 4 · Percentage change"},{"title":"Undo card","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M24 40 H70 A16 16 0 0 1 70 72 H40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3f5f45\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M34 30 L22 40 L34 50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3f5f45\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">÷ to undo ×</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>To find a whole from a part, find one share first.</b></p><p>⅖ of a number is 10. One fifth is 10 ÷ 2 = 5, so the whole is 5 × 5 = 25.</p><p>Check: ⅖ of 25 is 10.</p>","room":"The Returns Desk","lesson":"Lesson 5 · Reverse percentages"},{"title":"Interest ledger","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"14\" width=\"68\" height=\"74\" fill=\"#f3e6c4\" stroke=\"#8a6d40\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M16 32H84M16 50H84M16 68H84M44 14V88\" stroke=\"#8a6d40\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">Year</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">× 1.1</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">100</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">110</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b0412f\">121</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>Multiplying decimals: multiply the digits, then place the point.</b></p><p>1.2 × 1.2: 12 × 12 = 144, and there are two decimal places in all, so 1.2 × 1.2 = 1.44.</p>","room":"The Savings Bank","lesson":"Lesson 6 · Repeated change: compound interest and depreciation"},{"title":"Growth chart","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M14 84H90M14 84V12\" stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M14 80 L38 74 L62 62 L86 36\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3f8f4f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M14 80 L86 56\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f4f6b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\"/></svg>","body":"<p><b>Two ways to grow.</b></p><p>Adding the same amount: 5, 8, 11, 14 (add 3 each time).</p><p>Multiplying by the same amount: 2, 6, 18, 54 (multiply by 3 each time).</p>","room":"The Seedling Stall","lesson":"Lesson 7 · Growth models"},{"title":"Rounding line","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M10 60 H90\" stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M10 50V70M90 50V70M50 54V66\" stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"60\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#b0412f\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">2.6</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">2.7</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">2.65</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>To round to 1 decimal place, keep the tenths and look at the next digit.</b></p><p>2.68: the next digit after the 6 is 8, which is 5 or more, so 2.68 rounds up to 2.7.</p><p>2.63 rounds down to 2.6.</p>","room":"The Weights and Measures Office","lesson":"Lesson 8 · Bounds of a rounded value"},{"title":"Sharing strips","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"24\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#e7a3c4\" stroke=\"#7a3a5a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M30 24V40M50 24V40M70 24V40\" stroke=\"#7a3a5a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c3b1e1\" stroke=\"#4a3a7a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M50 60V76\" stroke=\"#4a3a7a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">fewer parts, bigger parts</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>Dividing by a smaller number gives a bigger answer.</b></p><p>20 ÷ 4 = 5 but 20 ÷ 5 = 4.</p><p>Sharing between fewer means each share is bigger.</p>","room":"The Fabric Stall","lesson":"Lesson 9 · Calculating with bounds"},{"title":"Speed triangle","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M50 14 L88 82 H12 Z\" fill=\"#f3e6c4\" stroke=\"#8a6d40\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M24 60 H76 M50 60 V82\" stroke=\"#8a6d40\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">D</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">S</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">T</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>Speed = distance ÷ time.</b></p><p>A cyclist rides 45 km in 3 hours: 45 ÷ 3 = 15 km/h.</p><p>Distance = speed × time, and time = distance ÷ speed.</p>","room":"The Delivery Bay","lesson":"Lesson 10 · Bounds in problems"}]};
